\section{The cache file}
\label{CacheFile}

The cache lives in one file per Canvas host, beside [[canvaslms]]'s own,
and is encrypted the same way: with a key derived from the Canvas token
and the host ([[derive_key]]).
It holds what students wrote and who they are, so it must be as safe as
[[canvaslms]]'s cache, which holds the same people; whoever has the token
can fetch all of it anyway.
A changed token makes the file unreadable, which we treat as an empty
cache: it costs one slow run, not an error.
The derivation takes a noticeable moment (PBKDF2, 100\,000 rounds), and we
need the key twice per run, so we keep it.

The content is JSON, not a pickle: the documents are JSON already, and a
file that cannot run code when it is read is one thing less to trust.
It records a schema version, and a file of another version is discarded.

What is written is pruned first: entries whose time has run out, entries
whose path no policy covers any more, and, when the user keeps personal
data out of [[canvaslms]]'s cache ([[cache.exclude: personal]], read
through [[excluded_kinds]]), every personal entry.
Then the course content stays, which is what makes a run fast with or
without the students' data.
A [[canvaslms]] from before the exclusion existed (6.24, which we still
accept) cannot exclude anything, so there everything may be written, as
[[canvaslms]]'s own cache does there.
The file is written to a temporary file and renamed, so that a run that
dies while writing leaves the old file, not half a new one.
The temporary file has a name of its own, so that two runs at once do not
write into each other's, and it is private from its creation
([[mkstemp]] makes it so), not only after a [[chmod]].
A file we cannot write, a full disk or a read-only directory, costs the
next run its speed, not this run its output: we warn, as [[canvaslms]] does
when it cannot save its own cache, and go on.

<<imports>>=
import functools
import os
import pathlib
import tempfile
from cryptography.fernet import Fernet, InvalidToken
import canvaslms
import canvaslms.cli
import canvaslms.cli.cache
<<constants>>=
SCHEMA_VERSION = 1
PERSONAL_KINDS = {"user", "submission"}
<<cache methods>>=
def snapshot(self, personal=True):
    """Return the entries worth keeping, personal ones only if allowed."""
    now = self.now()
    with self.lock:
        entries = dict(self.entries)
    kept = {}
    for key, entry in entries.items():
        policy = policy_of(entry["path"])
        if (policy is not None and now - entry["fetched"] <= policy.ttl
                and (personal or not policy.personal)):
            kept[key] = entry
    return kept
<<functions>>=
def cache_file(hostname):
    """Return the path of the cache file for a Canvas `hostname`."""
    safe = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9.-]", "_", hostname)
    return pathlib.Path(canvaslms.dirs.user_cache_dir) / f"fbf-{safe}.cache"


@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=4)
def fernet_for(token, hostname):
    """Return the encryption of the cache file for `token` and `hostname`."""
    return Fernet(canvaslms.cli.cache.derive_key(token, hostname))


def personal_allowed():
    """Whether personal data may go into the cache file."""
    excluded = getattr(canvaslms.cli.cache, "excluded_kinds", frozenset)
    return not PERSONAL_KINDS & set(excluded())


def load_cache(hostname, token, refresh=False, now=time.time, path=None):
    """Return the `Cache` stored for `hostname`, empty if there is none."""
    path = pathlib.Path(path or cache_file(hostname))
    try:
        payload = json.loads(
            fernet_for(token, hostname).decrypt(path.read_bytes()))
    except (OSError, InvalidToken, ValueError):
        payload = {}
    if not isinstance(payload, dict) or \
            payload.get("schema") != SCHEMA_VERSION:
        payload = {}
    return Cache(payload.get("entries"), payload.get("courses"), now=now,
                 refresh=refresh)


def save_cache(cache, hostname, token, path=None):
    """Write `cache` to the file for `hostname`, encrypted and pruned."""
    path = pathlib.Path(path or cache_file(hostname))
    payload = {"schema": SCHEMA_VERSION, "courses": cache.courses,
               "entries": cache.snapshot(personal_allowed())}
    data = fernet_for(token, hostname).encrypt(json.dumps(payload).encode())
    try:
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        handle, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=path.parent,
                                             prefix=path.name + ".")
        with os.fdopen(handle, "wb") as file:
            file.write(data)
        os.replace(temporary, path)
    except OSError as error:
        canvaslms.cli.warn(f"could not save the FeedbackFruits cache: {error}")
@

Let's verify the round trip and its refusals.
The file must not show the data in plain text, a file read with another
token or of another schema must give an empty cache, and expired entries
must not be written.
With personal data excluded, only the course content may be written.
The key derivation is the real one; we only set [[excluded_kinds]], which
is [[canvaslms]]'s configuration, not ours.

<<test functions>>=
def test_the_file_is_encrypted_and_survives_a_run(tmp_path,
                                                  personal_data_allowed):
  clock, path = Clock(), tmp_path / "fbf.cache"
  cache = Cache(courses={"5": "uuid-5"}, now=clock)
  cache.store("v1/people/u1/emails", {},
              {"data": [{"attributes": {"address": "ada@uni.example"}}]})
  save_cache(cache, "canvas.example", "token", path)
  assert b"ada@uni.example" not in path.read_bytes()
  assert path.stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o600
  assert [p.name for p in tmp_path.iterdir()] == ["fbf.cache"]
  loaded = load_cache("canvas.example", "token", now=clock, path=path)
  assert loaded.courses == {"5": "uuid-5"}
  assert loaded.lookup("v1/people/u1/emails", {}) is not None
  assert load_cache("canvas.example", "other token", path=path).entries == {}

def test_expired_and_unknown_schemas_are_dropped(tmp_path):
  clock, path = Clock(), tmp_path / "fbf.cache"
  cache = Cache(now=clock)
  cache.store("v1/progresses", {}, DOCUMENT)
  clock.time += LIST_TTL + 1
  save_cache(cache, "canvas.example", "token", path)
  assert load_cache("canvas.example", "token", path=path).entries == {}
  path.write_bytes(fernet_for("token", "canvas.example").encrypt(
    json.dumps({"schema": SCHEMA_VERSION + 1,
                "courses": {"5": "x"}}).encode()))
  assert load_cache("canvas.example", "token", path=path).courses == {}

def test_a_file_we_cannot_write_is_a_warning(tmp_path, caplog):
  blocked = tmp_path / "file"
  blocked.write_text("")
  save_cache(Cache(), "canvas.example", "token", blocked / "fbf.cache")
  assert "could not save the FeedbackFruits cache" in caplog.text

def test_personal_data_stays_out_when_excluded(tmp_path, monkeypatch):
  monkeypatch.setattr("canvaslms.cli.cache.excluded_kinds",
                      lambda: frozenset({"user", "group", "submission"}),
                      raising=False)
  path = tmp_path / "fbf.cache"
  cache = Cache()
  cache.store("v1/people/u1/emails", {}, DOCUMENT)
  cache.store("v1/activities/a", {"include": "tasks"}, DOCUMENT)
  save_cache(cache, "canvas.example", "token", path)
  loaded = load_cache("canvas.example", "token", path=path)
  assert [json.loads(key)[0] for key in loaded.entries] == ["v1/activities/a"]
