\section{The tokens}
\label{CacheTokens}

The launch is the one step we cannot cache as data: its result is a pair of
tokens (\cref{Launch}).
The access token is good for 30~minutes and the refresh token for 14~days,
and one pair serves all the user's courses, so a run that finds a pair from
an earlier run needs no launch at all, or one renewal (\cref{API}).
Tokens are credentials, so they go where [[canvaslms]] keeps the Canvas
token, in the system keyring, under the service [[fbf]] and the Canvas
host, and never into the cache file.
A system without a keyring simply launches every run, as before; that is
no reason to warn every run.

<<imports>>=
import keyring
import keyring.errors
from fbf.launch import FBFLogin
<<constants>>=
KEYRING_SERVICE = "fbf"
<<functions>>=
def stored_login(hostname):
    """Return the `FBFLogin` kept for `hostname`, or `None`."""
    try:
        text = keyring.get_password(KEYRING_SERVICE, hostname)
    except keyring.errors.KeyringError:
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(text or "")
        return FBFLogin(access_token=data["access_token"],
                        refresh_token=data["refresh_token"],
                        api_url=data["api_url"])
    except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return None


def store_login(hostname, login):
    """Keep the tokens of `login` for `hostname`, if there is a keyring."""
    try:
        keyring.set_password(KEYRING_SERVICE, hostname, json.dumps(
            {"access_token": login.access_token,
             "refresh_token": login.refresh_token,
             "api_url": login.api_url}))
    except keyring.errors.KeyringError:
        pass
@

Let's verify the round trip with a keyring of our own in memory, which is
the real [[keyring]] interface with a backend that keeps nothing beyond the
test, and that a keyring that fails is no error.
The viewer's tests need the same keyring (\cref{View}), so it is a shared
fixture; no test may touch the user's real keyring.
Likewise a test that expects personal data in the file sets
[[excluded_kinds]] itself, through [[personal_data_allowed]], since a developer
may well keep personal data out of their own cache with
[[CANVASLMS_CACHE_EXCLUDE]].

<<test fixtures>>=
import keyring
import keyring.backend


class MemoryKeyring(keyring.backend.KeyringBackend):
    """A keyring that keeps its passwords in memory, for one test."""

    priority = 1

    def __init__(self):
        self.passwords = {}

    def get_password(self, service, username):
        return self.passwords.get((service, username))

    def set_password(self, service, username, password):
        self.passwords[(service, username)] = password

    def delete_password(self, service, username):
        self.passwords.pop((service, username), None)


@pytest.fixture
def personal_data_allowed(monkeypatch):
    """Let personal data into the cache file, whatever the user set."""
    monkeypatch.setattr("canvaslms.cli.cache.excluded_kinds", frozenset,
                        raising=False)


@pytest.fixture
def memory_keyring():
    """Put a keyring in memory in place of the user's for one test."""
    before = keyring.get_keyring()
    keyring.set_keyring(MemoryKeyring())
    yield keyring.get_keyring()
    keyring.set_keyring(before)
